### Zig Version

0.11.0-dev.3031+f40539e5d

### Steps to Reproduce and Observed Behavior

The way the zig build test caching system works could lead to "tested" code defects getting missed. If zig thinks there was no change to the tests, it won't output any information. If someone isn't abnormally vigilant it could lead to tests going missing, where zig reports they were successfully executed. For the two example files/tests

A test is added, and tested
```zig
test "main.zig" {
    std.testing.refAllDecls(@This());
}
```
```zig
test "src/other.zig" {
    std.debug.assert(true);
}
```

user runs `zig build test -fsummary` and is told the build and test was successful.
```shell
Build Summary: 3/3 steps succeeded
test cached
└─ run test cached
   └─ zig test Debug native success 3s MaxRSS:244M
```

The user then makes a mistake, and somehow comments out some part of the testing env, perhaps during a refactor, or simply carelessness because they're working on a different file, and don't care about these tests.
```zig
test "main.zig" {
    //std.testing.refAllDecls(@This());
}
```
```zig
test "src/other.zig" {
    std.debug.assert(true);
}
```

